+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CE2KA7u9zXBLC7rkaa9dJj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RJjX1qL7jQg9chjD4g4MWb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/CONTRACT.md","content":"# CONTRACT — Constraint-Based Event Scheduler\n\nThe definition of done. Each criterion has a test that proves it.\n\n## API / Exports\n- [ ] `schedule(events, rooms, options)` is exported as a named export from `src/index.ts` -> test: import works, returns `{assignments, unscheduled}`.\n- [ ] Also available as default export and as `Scheduler` class / `createScheduler` factory -> test: all forms callable and equivalent.\n- [ ] All TypeScript interfaces (`Event`, `Room`, `ScheduleOptions`, `Assignment`, `ScheduleResult`) are exported -> test: build compiles, types importable.\n\n## Basic placement\n- [ ] A single event fits in a single room within the window -> test: 1 assignment, 0 unscheduled, start>=startTime, end<=endTime, end-start==duration.\n- [ ] `attendees` defaults to 1 when omitted (placeable in capacity-1 room) -> test: event with no attendees placed in capacity-1 room.\n- [ ] Returned assignment endTime == startTime + duration -> test: arithmetic check.\n\n## Rule 1 — Room capacity\n- [ ] Event with attendees > capacity of every room is unscheduled -> test: attendees=100, all rooms cap<100 => unscheduled contains event.\n- [ ] Event placed only in a room whose capacity >= attendees -> test: two rooms, only the big one is used.\n- [ ] attendees == capacity is allowed (boundary) -> test: attendees=10 in cap=10 room placed.\n\n## Rule 2 — Time window\n- [ ] Every assignment satisfies startTime>=options.startTime and endTime<=options.endTime -> test: invariant over all assignments.\n- [ ] Event whose duration exceeds the window is unscheduled -> test: duration > endTime-startTime => unscheduled.\n- [ ] Event ending exactly at endTime is allowed (boundary) -> test: duration == window => placed ending at endTime.\n\n## Rule 3 — Room gaps\n- [ ] Two events in same room are separated by at least `gap` minutes (next.start - prev.end >= gap) -> test: invariant holds for co-room events.\n- [ ] Default gap is 15 when not provided -> test: two events forced same room => >=15 min apart.\n- [ ] gap=0 allows back-to-back events -> test: events touch with 0 gap.\n- [ ] Custom gap respected -> test: gap=30 => >=30 min separation.\n\n## Rule 4 — Prerequisites\n- [ ] If B requires A, A.end + gap <= B.start in result -> test: invariant for prereq pairs (across rooms too).\n- [ ] B cannot be scheduled if its prerequisite A is unscheduled -> test: A unschedulable => B in unscheduled.\n- [ ] Missing/unknown prerequisite id makes the event unscheduled (cannot be satisfied) -> test: prereq id not in events => unscheduled, no throw.\n- [ ] Chain A->B->C respects ordering with gaps -> test: A.end+gap<=B.start, B.end+gap<=C.start.\n\n## Rule 5 — Preferred room\n- [ ] When preferredRoom is feasible without reducing scheduled count, the event lands there -> test: event placed in its preferredRoom.\n- [ ] Preferred room is a hint: if infeasible there, event still placed elsewhere -> test: preferred room too small => placed in another room, still scheduled.\n\n## Rule 6 — Cycles (throw)\n- [ ] Self-reference A->A throws -> test: expect(()=>schedule(...)).toThrow().\n- [ ] Two-node cycle A->B->A throws -> test: throws.\n- [ ] Longer cycle A->B->C->A throws -> test: throws.\n- [ ] A valid DAG does NOT throw -> test: no throw.\n\n## Rule 7 — Batch optimization (maximize scheduled)\n- [ ] Naive in-order placement is beaten: scenario where greedy schedules fewer than optimal; scheduler finds the max -> test: constructed case where smart packing schedules all/more.\n- [ ] All events placed when capacity allows -> test: everything schedulable => unscheduled empty.\n- [ ] Events that genuinely cannot fit go to unscheduled, no throw -> test: over-subscribed window => some unscheduled, rest valid.\n\n## General invariants (always hold on any result)\n- [ ] Every event id appears exactly once: either in assignments or unscheduled (partition) -> test: union==all ids, disjoint, no dupes.\n- [ ] No two events overlap (with gap) in the same room -> test: invariant.\n- [ ] Empty events array => empty result -> test: {assignments:[],unscheduled:[]}.\n- [ ] No rooms => everything unscheduled -> test.\n- [ ] Result never mutates input arrays/objects -> test: deep-equal inputs before/after.\n\n## Quality gates\n- [ ] `npm test` passes (all tests green).\n- [ ] `npm run build` compiles with no errors.\n- [ ] `npm run lint` reports no errors.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":277,"cache_read_input_tokens":24743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":277},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b8f80fc-1370-4005-9176-89c983cc0f4d","uuid":"4af125b1-610b-4007-8cc3-30b3947eccf5","request_id":"req_011CbWGybanE4vyuEJMn1ABw"}
